# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Build context for the OnTrak Sentinel image.
#
# Two rules: never copy in what the image installs or generates itself, and
# never let local state or a secret reach a layer. Nothing excluded here is
# needed by the build.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and regenerated inside the image
**/node_modules
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Compose injects these at run time; a layer would freeze them forever.
# `SENTINEL_SIGNING_KEY` is the one that matters most here: it is the key every
# ID token is signed with, and baking it into an image publishes it to everyone
# who can pull the image.
.env
.env*.local
*.pem
*.key

# Repository tooling and the image definition itself
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
test-results
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
